<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azarmidokht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 631 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azarmidokht was a Sasanian queen who ruled briefly around 630–631, during a period of rapid succession after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a>. She was one of two women, with her sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boran">Boran</a>, to occupy the Sasanian throne. Her short reign reflects the political chaos that weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> shortly before the Arab conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azarmidokht.jpg" alt="Azarmidokht" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AzarmidokhtCoinHistoryofIran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
